<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="3c0ad975">The Change Control Plan sets expectations on how the approach to changes will be managed, what defines a change, the
purpose and role of the change control board, and the overall change management process. All stakeholders will be expected
to submit or request changes in accordance with this work product and all requests and submissions will follow
the process detailed within the approved plan.</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="94a83ddf"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="e2b38d32"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="348cd3b8"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="2401f9fa">To set expectations on how the approach to changes will be managed.&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="3360a7a"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="382e43c"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="fb1e8641">&lt;p&gt;
    The Change Control Plan should contain:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Approach to managing change
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Definitions of Change - Types of changes, their criteria and allowable states
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Change Control Process, procedures and corresponding workflow 
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Exception process
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Levels of authority, including Change Control Boards or other bodies, and their roles and
        responsibilities 
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Change limits
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Change tracking and reporting (including communicating back to submitters)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="f30cc084"></attribute>
<attribute name="representation" nodeId="fb8075fc"></attribute>
